   "description": "<p><strong>Role Title: </strong>STEM Expert – Chemistry &amp; Computational Chemistry (PhD)</p><p><strong>Role Type: </strong>Contractor</p><p><strong>Location:</strong> Remote (Worldwide)</p><p><strong>Job Summary:</strong> In this role, you’ll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input.</p><h3>Key Responsibilities:</h3><ol>\n<li>Design, evaluate, and critique chemistry and computational chemistry problems, workflows, and reasoning chains to support AI benchmarking initiatives.</li>\n<li>Provide expert-level insights on reaction mechanisms, synthesis planning, spectroscopy analysis, molecular simulations, and electronic structure methods.</li>\n<li>Assess and optimize experimental protocols, simulation parameters, and software configurations for accuracy and reproducibility.</li>\n<li>Analyze chemical, spectroscopic, and simulation data and provide actionable recommendations.</li>\n<li>Leverage domain knowledge to guide the development and validation of chemistry-related AI models and tools.</li>\n<li>Communicate complex scientific concepts clearly, both in writing and verbally, to technical and non-technical collaborators.</li>\n<li>Document findings, methodologies, and best practices to ensure knowledge transfer across the customer’s team.</li>\n</ol><p><strong>Areas of Expertise (we welcome applicants from any of the following):</strong></p><ol>\n<li>Organic synthesis &amp; reaction mechanisms</li>\n<li>Inorganic &amp; organometallic chemistry</li>\n<li>Physical &amp; theoretical chemistry</li>\n<li>Analytical chemistry &amp; spectroscopy</li>\n<li>Computational chemistry &amp; molecular dynamics</li>\n<li>Cheminformatics &amp; drug discovery</li>\n<li>Materials science &amp; polymer chemistry</li>\n</ol><h3>Required Skills and Qualifications:</h3><ol>\n<li>\n<strong>PhD</strong> in chemistry, computational chemistry, chemical biology, materials science, or a closely related field.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Hands-on research lab experience</strong>, including wet lab experience for experimental subfields, or extensive simulation-heavy research for computational subfields.</li>\n<li>Deep expertise in at least one of the areas listed above.</li>\n<li>Professional written and spoken English (C1 or higher).</li>\n<li>Proficiency in Python and/or industry-standard tools in your subfield (e.g., Gaussian, ORCA, Psi4, GROMACS, LAMMPS, RDKit).</li>\n<li>Excellent quantitative, analytical, and scientific reasoning skills.</li>\n<li>Outstanding written and verbal communication abilities, with the ability to clearly document and explain technical concepts.</li>\n<li>Track record of rigorous scientific problem-solving in complex chemistry domains.</li>\n</ol><h3>Preferred Qualifications:</h3><ol>\n<li>\n<strong>Academic experience</strong> (postdoc, research scientist, faculty, or equivalent), strongly preferred.</li>\n<li>Peer-reviewed publications, patents, or contributions to open-source scientific software.</li>\n<li>Experience with AI/ML-assisted chemistry workflows or benchmarking.</li>\n<li>Background in drug discovery, reaction prediction, or retrosynthesis.</li>\n</ol><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
