   "description": "<p><strong>Job Title:</strong> STEM Expert – Biology &amp; Bioinformatics (PhD)</p><p><strong>Job Type:</strong> Contractor</p><p><strong>Location:</strong> Remote(Worldwide)</p><p><strong>Job Summary:</strong> In this role, you’ll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input.</p><h3>Key Responsibilities:</h3><ol>\n<li>Design, evaluate, and critique biology, bioinformatics, and computational biology workflows to support AI benchmarking initiatives.</li>\n<li>Provide expert-level insights on genomic, transcriptomic, proteomic, and other biological data analysis pipelines.</li>\n<li>Assess and optimize pipeline parameters, tool configurations, and statistical methods for accuracy and reproducibility.</li>\n<li>Analyze biological datasets (e.g., NGS, RNA-seq, single-cell, variant calling, protein structure) and provide actionable recommendations.</li>\n<li>Leverage domain knowledge to guide the development and validation of biology-related AI models and tools.</li>\n<li>Communicate complex scientific concepts clearly, both in writing and verbally, to technical and non-technical collaborators.</li>\n<li>Document findings, methodologies, and best practices to ensure knowledge transfer across the customer’s team.</li>\n</ol><p><strong>Areas of Expertise (we welcome applicants from any of the following):</strong></p><ol>\n<li>Genomics &amp; NGS analysis</li>\n<li>Transcriptomics &amp; single-cell analysis</li>\n<li>Proteomics &amp; structural biology</li>\n<li>Molecular &amp; cell biology</li>\n<li>Systems biology &amp; biological network analysis</li>\n<li>Drug discovery &amp; computational pharmacology</li>\n<li>Biostatistics &amp; machine learning applied to biology</li>\n</ol><h3>Required Skills and Qualifications:</h3><ol>\n<li>PhD in biology, bioinformatics, computational biology, genomics, or a closely related STEM field, or equivalent industry/research experience.</li>\n<li>Professional written and spoken English (C1 or higher).</li>\n<li>Deep expertise in at least one of the areas listed above, with hands-on experience analyzing real biological data.</li>\n<li>Proficiency in Python and/or R for scientific analysis, plus experience with standard tools in your subfield (e.g., BLAST, samtools, GATK, Bioconductor, Biopython).</li>\n<li>Strong statistical, quantitative, and analytical reasoning skills.</li>\n<li>Outstanding written and verbal communication abilities, with the ability to clearly document and explain technical concepts.</li>\n<li>Track record of rigorous scientific problem-solving in complex biological domains.</li>\n</ol><h3>Preferred Qualifications:</h3><ol>\n<li>Experience building reproducible workflows (Nextflow, Snakemake) and working in Linux/command-line environments.</li>\n<li>Experience with AI/ML-assisted biology workflows or benchmarking.</li>\n<li>Peer-reviewed publications, patents, or contributions to open-source bioinformatics software.</li>\n</ol><p>Originally posted on <a href=\"https://himalayas.app\">Himalayas</a></p>",
